L_{\text{lasso}}(\beta)
 =\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(y_i-\hat y_i\right)^{2}
 +\lambda\sum_{j=1}^{p}\left|\beta_j\right|

Ridge:\quad
 \hat\beta_j=\frac{\hat\beta_j^{\text{OLS}}}{1+\lambda}
 \qquad\text{— $\lambda$ in the denominator: division.}

Lasso:\quad
 \hat\beta_j=\operatorname{sign} \left(\hat\beta_j^{\text{OLS}}\right)
 \left(\left|\hat\beta_j^{\text{OLS}}\right|-\frac{\lambda}{2}\right)_{ +}
 \qquad\text{— $\lambda$ subtracted.}

\partial|\beta| =
 \begin{cases}
 {+1} & \beta>0

 [-1,1] & \beta=0

 {-1} & \beta<0 .
 \end{cases}

items:
Limitations: with correlated features it picks one arbitrarily;
 it can select at most $n$ features when $p>n$; and the selected set is not
 guaranteed to be the true model.
